## 3. C# in Comparison

| Feature | C# | C++ | Java | Python |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Typing** | Static, Strong | Static, Strong | Static, Strong | Dynamic, Strong |
| **Execution** | Managed (CLR + JIT/AOT) | Native (Ahead of Time) | Managed (JVM + JIT) | Interpreted (Bytecode) |
| **Memory** | Automatic GC (+ manual primitives)[cite: 10] | Manual (`malloc`/`new`)[cite: 10] | Automatic GC | Automatic GC |
| **Primary Sweet Spot** | Web APIs, Enterprise, Cloud, Games[cite: 4] | Systems, Drivers, High-Perf Engines | Enterprise Backends, Big Data | Data Science, Scripting, AI Prototyping |

---

## 4. Key Takeaways

* **C#** is a statically typed, multi-paradigm, managed programming language designed for reliability and speed[cite: 4, 10].
* It powers every layer of modern software: Web APIs, Cloud, Desktop, Mobile, AI, and Games[cite: 4].
* It combines developer ergonomics (memory safety, LINQ, clean syntax) with systems-level performance controls (`Span<T>`, Native AOT)[cite: 8, 10].
